## A Quick Introduction to Copilot Studio

Microsoft Copilot Studio is a low-code platform for building AI-powered agents inside the Microsoft 365 ecosystem. Unlike the Copilot button baked into Word or Excel, Copilot Studio lets you design custom agents that chain multiple steps together: reading a file, processing its contents, calling an AI model, and writing outputs back to OneDrive, Teams, or wherever you need them. It connects natively to Office apps, Power Automate, and SharePoint, which makes it a natural fit for finance and analytics workflows that already live in the Microsoft stack.

*[Link: Microsoft Copilot Studio overview -- https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-copilot/microsoft-copilot-studio]*

The strengths are real: low barrier to entry, tight M365 integration, and the ability to combine structured data processing with AI reasoning in one workflow. The limitations are also worth knowing upfront. Multi-step agents can be slow on complex workflows, the Excel connector works best with clean and well-structured tables, large files can hit context limits, and the licensing cost adds up if agents run at scale. With that said, for repeatable analytical tasks, it's a genuinely capable platform. Now let's get into a concrete example.

